From 2852da09c6b234eeadcfda0636a4a773c208186a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mpenelange <191051681+mpenelange@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:50:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] Build on Linux 5.15 (Oracle UEK7) as well as 5.4

- ipfwd_compat.h: /proc files use struct proc_ops since 5.6; all 32
  file_operations structs go through ipfwd_proc_ops/IPFWD_PROC_* macros
- platform_bonding.c: bond->rr_tx_counter is per-CPU since 5.12

Tested: loads and fast-paths on UEK7 5.15.0-er4 (ER-4, 824 kpps 64-byte
routed, 0 drops, 29% CPU); still builds against UEK6 5.4.17-er4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
